-- A language tag that nothing else backs. The rule has no other wording, no
-- other wording in the module is in `the`, and no `@lang` line declares it, so
-- `the` is almost certainly the first word of the sentence and not a language.
-- The wording is attached either way; the diagnostic says what to write.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `over limit` @nlg:the claim of %amount% is over the limit
  IF amount GREATER THAN 100
